assistant: Subject: parse epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

The flagged alert (the 404) is not caused by shop-mcp, and this change doesn't fix it. create_order passed through exactly what the vendor's `POST /orders` returned, and the vendor itself answered 404 to `GET /orders/o-5002`. Nothing in our code changes that request, and I couldn't find a cause in this repo, so the order should stay "unconfirmed" and the 404 needs to go to the vendor. The recorded response did show a real bug, though: vendor version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as epoch milliseconds (`1792315539045`) instead of the ISO-8601 string the spec promises. get_order ran that number through `Date.parse(String(...))`, which gave NaN and then 0, so once the read-back works it would report every order as placed on 1970-01-01. get_order now uses a numeric `created_at` directly as epoch ms and still parses strings as before, so v1 output is unchanged. Typecheck, lint and tests pass, but they only use the v1 fixtures, so the new number path hasn't been run by any test.

